@startuml
class Session {
  id: UUID
  activityCode: string (unique)
  currentRoundId: UUID?
  stateVersion: integer
  createdAt: UTC timestamp
}
class Round {
  id: UUID
  sessionId: UUID
  questionId: UUID?
  questionGroupId: UUID?
  phase: Waiting | Active | Ended
  createdAt: UTC timestamp
  startedAt: UTC timestamp?
  endedAt: UTC timestamp?
}
class Question {
  id: UUID
  sessionId: UUID
  questionGroupId: UUID?
  displayNumber: string?
  prompt: string?
  position: integer
}
class Blank {
  id: UUID
  questionId: UUID
  label: string?
  position: integer
}
class QuestionGroup {
  id: UUID
  sessionId: UUID
  label: string?
  position: integer
}
class Team {
  id: UUID
  sessionId: UUID
  name: string
}
class Participant {
  id: UUID
  teamId: UUID
  displayName: string?
}
class Submission {
  id: UUID
  teamId: UUID
  roundId: UUID
  receivedAt: UTC timestamp
  acceptedOrder: integer
}
class SubmissionAnswer {
  submissionId: UUID
  blankId: UUID
  value: string
}
class Result {
  id: UUID
  roundId: UUID (unique)
  winningSubmissionId: UUID (unique)
  createdAt: UTC timestamp
}
Session "1" o-- "0..*" Round
Session "0..1" --> "0..1" Round : currentRoundId
Session "1" o-- "0..*" Question
Session "1" o-- "0..*" QuestionGroup
Session "1" o-- "0..*" Team
Round "0..*" --> "0..1" Question
Round "0..*" --> "0..1" QuestionGroup
Question "1" o-- "0..*" Blank
QuestionGroup "0..1" o-- "1..*" Question
Team "1" o-- "0..*" Participant
Team "1" --> "0..*" Submission
Round "1" --> "0..*" Submission
Submission "1" o-- "0..*" SubmissionAnswer
Blank "1" --> "0..*" SubmissionAnswer
Round "1" --> "0..1" Result
Submission "1" --> "0..1" Result
note right of Round
A Round targets exactly one Question XOR one QuestionGroup.
A logical target may have multiple historical Rounds.
New target/reopen creates Waiting; Start activates that same Round.
Scoped foreign keys require its Question/QuestionGroup and its Session current pointer to belong to the same Session.
end note
note bottom of Submission
Unique Team + Round prevents duplicate successful submissions.
acceptedOrder is assigned by the server within the Round.
Team and Round must be in the same Session; SubmissionAnswer Blanks must belong to the Round target.
A Result references a winning Submission from its own Round.
end note
note bottom of Session
A new Session may have no Rounds or Teams.
No current Round means Waiting.
stateVersion increments after observable state changes.
end note
note right of Question
0..* Blanks is intentional per FR-005.
A zero-Blank target is valid data; Student Feature rejects submission.
end note
note bottom of Result
On new-round completion, replace the previous Result
for the same Question or QuestionGroup in one transaction.
end note
@enduml
